---
alwaysApply: true
---
rules:

    general:
        - Functions must be under 25 lines.
        - Compile with: `-Wall -Wextra -Werror`.
        - No memory leaks, no file descriptor leaks, no undefined behavior.
        - Keep code modular and organized in proper folders (parsing, movement, render, init, exit, debug).

    allowed-functions:
        - open, close, read, write
        - printf, perror, strerror
        - malloc, free, exit
        - gettimeofday
        - All math library functions (-lm)
        - All MiniLibX functions

    forbidden:
        - Any libc functions outside the allowed list (no calloc, realloc, strdup, getline, etc.).
        - Any system calls such as fork, execve, pipe, sockets, or threads.
        - Any external libraries.
        - Any C++ code.

    code-requirements:
        - Always check and handle errors (file opening, allocation failures, MLX failures).
        - Use header files for prototypes, structures, and macros.
        - Maintain clear separation between parsing, rendering, raycasting, and utilities.

    behavior:
    - Implement all features exactly as defined in the Cub3D subject.
    - Correctly manage MiniLibX lifecycle: init, images, window, hooks, and clean shutdown.
